*.sh text eol=lf

# The tracked-ai/ ratchet no longer keeps a committed baseline snapshot
# (rf2-ow7dz): it reads its base state straight from git, so there is no
# checked-out list for a Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checkout to
# CRLF-normalise and no EOL pin to carry here.

# The git-hook sources (post-merge, post-rewrite, pre-commit) are POSIX sh but
# carry no .sh extension, so the rule above misses them. Pin them to LF so the
# checked-out source matches the LF-normalised installed hook byte-for-byte
# on the line-ending axis, and so the `sh -n` parse / `dash` checks never see
# a stray CR on a Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checkout (rf2-ujhpf).
scripts/git-hooks/post-merge text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/post-rewrite text eol=lf
scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit text eol=lf

# The docs/cljs playground BOOTSTRAP bundles are committed, vendored prebuilts
# that esbuild emits with LF endings (rf2-ee38b.22). Pin LF so a Windows
# checkout / rebuild never CRLF-normalises them — that would make the CI
# bundle-drift gate (tools-playground) `git diff` against a fresh Linux build
# spuriously fail.
#
# docs/cljs/playground-rf2.js is deliberately absent (rf2-tzy13): the shadow-cljs
# SCI bundle is no longer tracked — it is .gitignored and generated in CI and on
# docs deploy — so it is never diffed and needs no EOL pin.
docs/cljs/playground.js text eol=lf
docs/cljs/playground.css text eol=lf
# Pin the source CSS to LF too: `copy-css.mjs` copies it byte-for-byte to the
# committed docs/cljs/playground.css, so a CRLF source would yield a CRLF
# output and trip the drift gate.
docs/tools/playground/src/playground.css text eol=lf

# The generated public-API manifest + its curated sidecar (rf2-3nbl5.2). The
# generator writes LF-normalised bytes and the CI drift-check regenerates on
# Linux; pin LF so a Windows (core.autocrlf=true) checkout never CRLF-rewrites
# the committed file and trips a spurious manifest drift.
spec/api-manifest.edn text eol=lf
spec/api-manifest-metadata.edn text eol=lf

# The generated MCP tool-descriptor manifests (rf2-sofwv). Each MCP server
# generates its committed manifest from the live tool registry; CI drift-checks
# it on Linux. Pin LF — same rationale as the api-manifest above — so a Windows
# checkout never CRLF-rewrites the committed file and trips a spurious drift.
tools/story-mcp/tool-descriptors.edn text eol=lf
tools/re-frame2-pair-mcp/tool-descriptors.edn text eol=lf

# The generated re-frame.ui AI context sheet (rf2-u53yy.8). Its compile-rejection
# roster is generated from the compiler's didactic messages; CI drift-checks the
# committed file on Linux. Pin LF — same rationale as the api-manifest above — so
# a Windows checkout never CRLF-rewrites it and trips a spurious drift.
skills/re-frame2-ui/references/ui-context.md text eol=lf

# The outside-instrument evidence, retained byte-exact (rf2-rguy1). These two
# files are cited by their SHA-256 on the studio page that reads them, so the
# digest is the artefact and any re-writing destroys it. A Windows
# (core.autocrlf=true) checkout would CRLF-rewrite them and a reader there
# would compute a different hash from the one the page names. Pin LF.
implementation/freehand/test/re_frame/bench/hicasso/data/jsfb-rguy1/*.json text eol=lf
